  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Palantir Usg has federal contract obligations of $1.2B in FY2026 to date. Palantir Usg won 66 awards so far, with an average award size of $18.8M and obligations that are up 66.9% year over year. Department of Defense is the largest buyer; the Department of Defense obligated $1.2B for Palantir Usg in FY2026 to date. Contract activity increased across multiple recent fiscal years: Palantir Usg obligations were $67.6M in FY21, $198M in FY22, $151M in FY23, $288M in FY24, and $745M in FY25, before reaching $1.2B in FY26. Palantir Usg sells primarily in Custom Computer Programming Services and Software Publishers, with Custom Computer Programming Services totaling $1B and Software Publishers totaling $181M in FY2026 to date. Other identified markets include Other Management Consulting Services at $27.1M, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $247K, and a second Software Publishers entry at $236K. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Palantir Usg’s FY2026 federal spending compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Palantir Usg obligations rose to $1.2B in FY26, up from $745M in FY25 and $288M in FY24. Palantir Usg obligations were $151M in FY23, $198M in FY22, and $67.6M in FY21. Palantir Usg obligations are up 66.9% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top federal buyers and what markets does Palantir Usg serve?",
        "body": "Department of Defense is the top buyer, with obligations of $1.2B in FY2026 to date. Department of State obligated $56.2M, National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $12.1M, and U.S. International Development Finance Corporation obligated $8.1M. Palantir Usg sells mainly in Custom Computer Programming Services ($1B) and Software Publishers ($181M), with additional activity in Other Management Consulting Services ($27.1M) and smaller R&D and software publisher segments ($247K and $236K respectively)."
      }
    ]
